'''''Nyanko Daisensou''''' was a tower-defense and strategy game developed by [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] and released for Japanese mobile phones in 2010. On November 15th, 2012, it was [[Nyanko Daisensou|re-released]] for iOS devices under the same name but with more content and polish, the old version renamed to '''''Ganso! Nyanko Daisensou'''''. The same day, this updated version was made available outside of Japan under the name '''''Battle Cats''''' from November 15th, 2012 to January 10th, 2013, when it was last updated and was removed from both the Google Play Store and the App Store. On September 17th, 2014, the English version reappeared under the name '''''The Battle Cats'''''.

==Games==
===Main===
The main game has two main servers, Japanese and International. The Japanese Version has been updated from version 1.0 to this day. However the International Version, which was separated later, was removed abruptly at version 1.5. Then it continues at version 2.0 as a separate game.

*''[[Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou]]'': The original, subscription-based Japanese version, which had only one chapter and the [[Higher Score|Challenge Battle]]. The first nine [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] were the only units available. Originally just called ''Nyanko Daisensou'', it was later renamed with the prefix ''Ganso!!'' (meaning "original") to distinguish itself from the new version.
*''[[Nyanko Daisensou]]'': The updated Japanese re-release, a free-to-play game available on iOS and Android devices. Has many new features compared to the original, beginning with [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]] and two additional chapters.
**''Tobidasu! Nyanko Daisensou'': The Nintendo 3DS version of ''Nyanko Daisensou''.
**''Futari de! Nyanko Daisensou'': The Nintendo Switch version of ''Nyanko Daisensou''.
**''[[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou]]''<sup>removed</sup>: The PC version of ''Nyanko Daisensou''. Defunct as of January 31st, 2019.
*''[[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]]''<sup>removed</sup>: The old English version, which was an alternative version of ''Nyanko Daisensou''.
*''[[The Battle Cats]]'': The current, updated English version, also known as ''Battle Cats'' version 2.
**''[[The Battle Cats POP!]]'': The Nintendo 3DS version of ''The Battle Cats''.
**''[[The Battle Cats Unite!]]'': The Nintendo Switch version of ''The Battle Cats''.
*''Nyangko Daejeonjaeng'' (냥코 대전쟁): The Korean version, roughly translates to ''Nyanko Great War''. Very similar to the English version, but with minor differences; see [[Regional Differences]] for more information.
*''Māomī Dàzhànzhēng'' (貓咪大戰爭): The Chinese/Taiwanese version, roughly translates to ''Nyanko Great War''. Shares most of its content with the English and Korean versions.

===Spin-offs===
*''[[Nyanko Daibōsō]]'' (にゃんこ大暴走)<sup>removed</sup>: A runner game developed by PONOS and DeNA Co Ltd. Defunct as of November 28th, 2014.
*''[[Kumanchu Royale]]'' (クマんちゅ ロワイアル)<sup>removed</sup>: A bear-themed sequel/spin-off to ''Ganso! Nyanko Daisensou''. Discontinued alongside its prequel on January 6th, 2015.
*''[[Battle Cats Rangers]]'' (にゃんこレンジャー)<sup>removed</sup>: A clicker spin-off title that was released by MEMORY Inc. on April 17th, 2017. Defunct as of March 29th, 2019.
*''[[Go! Go! Pogo Cat]]'': An endless runner game starring [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Pogo Cat]] and other familiar [[Cat Units]].
*''[[Nyanko Defence Force|Nyanko Bōei-gun]]'' (にゃんこ防衛軍)<sup>removed</sup>: A space shooter available as a LINE quick game. Developed by PONOS and Game Closure. Defunct as of October 30th, 2020.
*''[[The Burgle Cats]]'' (にゃんこ大泥棒): A spin-off which has the cats breaking into a manor while protecting their own from other burglars.
*''[[Nyanko New Japan|Nyanko Shin Nihon]]'' (にゃんこ新日本): A puzzle spin-off made to commemorate the 8th anniversary of ''Nyanko Daisensou''.
*''[[Battle Cats Quest]]'' (にゃんこクエスト): A ''Battle Cats'' reskin of one of PONOS' other games, ''Ball Action''.
*''[[Puzzle Bonanza! Nyanko Village|Pazuru de Hōsaku！Nyanko Mura]]'' (パズルで豊作！にゃんこ村): A match 3 puzzle game.

===Related Games===
*The ''Mr.'' series<sup>removed</sup>: A discontinued series of puzzle games whose [[Mr. (Special Cat)|titular character]] is a purchasable [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]].
*''[[GirlsMons]]'' (ガルズモンズ)<sup>removed</sup>: A puzzle-based RPG that had some of its characters ([[Undead Cat (Special Cat)|Undead Cat]] and the [[Girls & Monsters: Angels of Terror (Gacha Event)|Girls & Monsters]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]]) permanently added to The Battle Cats as playable units.
*''Namesta'' (なめすた)<sup>removed</sup>: A slug racing game whose slimy steeds appear in The Battle Cats as [[Slug Jockey Cat (Rare Cat)|Slug Jockey Cat]] and [[Red Slug|the]] [[Black Slug|Slug]][[Angelic Slug|gies]].
*''[[Kyoutou Project]]'' (京刀のナユタ)<sup>removed</sup>: A story-based tower defense game whose protagonist [[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]] is obtainable as a [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cat]] in The Battle Cats.
*''[[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarō: Yōkai Dotabata Daisensō]]'' (ゆる～いゲゲゲの鬼太郎 妖怪ドタバタ大戦争) or simply '''YuruGeGe''' (ゆるゲゲ)<sup>removed</sup>: A [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:GeGeGe no Kitarō Wiki|GeGeGe no Kitarō]] tower defense game developed by PONOS and DeNa. Although its characters have only been obtainable as part of a [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou Collaboration Event|collab]], some of its exclusive features may have inspired those in The Battle Cats or were later added directly, such as the "show and deploy from both rows at once" option in [[Battle|battles]].
